message.content:
Sure! Those coordinates point to the Googleplex in Mountain View, California.

If you query the Google Geocoding API with:

```
https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json?latlng=37.4224764,-122.0842499&key=YOUR_API_KEY
```

you’ll receive a JSON response that includes (among other details):

```json
{
  "results": [
    {
      "formatted_address": "1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA",
      "geometry": {
        "location": {
          "lat": 37.4224764,
          "lng": -122.0842499
        },
        ...
      }
    }
  ],
  "status": "OK"
}
```

So the latitude and longitude are exactly **37.4224764** and **‑122.0842499**, which correspond to the Google headquarters address.
